  "summary": "Krasue is a Linux Remote Access Trojan (RAT) primarily targeting telecommunications companies in Thailand. It features an embedded rootkit, based on several open-source projects, to hide its presence by hooking syscalls and hiding files, processes, and network ports. Krasue maintains persistence and communicates with its C2 server using AES-encrypted traffic over UDP and a distinctive RTSP-based 'alive ping'.",
